# NOTICE

This project is a derivative work.

## Upstream

`reverse-engineering-distribution` started from the source of
[reverse-engineer-marketing](https://github.com/dansugc/reverse-engineer-marketing)
by Daniel Hangan (DansUGC), MIT licensed, version 0.1.0.

That project was itself inspired by [REA, Reverse Engineer
Anything](https://github.com/morluto/rea).

## What was inherited

The evidence contract (observation / derivation / unknown), the collector
sources for website forensics, tracking pixels and GTM containers, SEO and
sitemaps, AI-crawler stance, Wayback history, App Store / Play, Hacker News,
the paid and social collectors, the harness loader, the report writer engines,
the MCP server scaffolding, the web app and the 23 parser/security tests.

## What is original to this work

- The distribution lens: what is new is the question the bundle answers.
- `src/sources/communities.ts`: Atom feed parsing, community measurement
  (cadence, link share, promo share, question share), rule classification,
  the five verdicts and the gate logic.
- `src/analyze/plan.ts`: the deterministic 7/30-day distribution plan, the
  closed and unconfirmed lists.
- The rewritten harness: distribution analyst role, rules-first guardrails,
  the distribution report template, a new lesson library, nine surface
  playbooks, and a new validator (required sections, plan grounding, "every
  audited community got a verdict").
- The CLI/MCP surface under the `red` name, and the additional tests
  (communities, plan, harness, validator) that bring the suite to 66.

